            "NaCl",
            "Na$$_2$$SO$$_4$$",
            "Na$$_2$$S"
          ],
          "correct": 3,
          "explanation": "<p>The compound <b>X</b> is H$$_2$$S:</p>\n<p>$$\\mathrm{\\mathop {N{a_2}S}\\limits_{(X)}  + 2{H^ + } \\to {H_2}S + 2N{a^ + }}$$</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/@width/image/1lfrmykpg/613c0862-dbf6-4cfd-9751-3b21c73340e1/d0860140-cd0f-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrmykph.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lfrmykpg/613c0862-dbf6-4cfd-9751-3b21c73340e1/d0860140-cd0f-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrmykph.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 0px auto; max-height: 40vh;\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Salt Analysis Question 3 English Explanation 1\"></p>\n<p>Thus, the compound <b>Y</b> is FeCl$$_3$$.</p>\n<p>Compound <b>Y</b> on reaction with potassium hyxacyanoferrate(II) forms intense blue precipitate which dissolves on addition of reagent</p>\n<p>$$\\mathrm{4FeC{l_3} + 3{K_4}\\left[ {Fe(II){{(CN)}_6}} \\right] \\to \\mathop {F{e_4}{{[Fe{{(CN)}_6}]}_3}}\\limits_{Intense\\,blue\\,ppt.}  + 12KCl}$$</p>\n<p>Compound <b>Y</b> on reaction with potassium hexacyanoferrate (III) forms brown colouration due to</p>\n<p>$$\\mathrm{Fe[Fe(CN)_6]}$$</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/@width/image/1lfrn09qx/a2aeb4d3-d055-4010-9fb4-a79e884eb02b/ffad1490-cd0f-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrn09qy.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lfrn09qx/a2aeb4d3-d055-4010-9fb4-a79e884eb02b/ffad1490-cd0f-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrn09qy.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 0px auto; max-height: 40vh;\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Salt Analysis Question 3 English Explanation 2\"></p>"
        },
