          "question": "The metal rod M is",
          "image_url": null,
          "options": [
            "Fe",
            "Cu",
            "Ni",
            "Co"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p>M is copper and N is silver nitrate according to the equation</p>\n<p>$$\\mathop {Cu}\\limits_{(M)}  + \\mathop {2AgN{O_3}}\\limits_{(N)}  \\to \\mathop {Cu{{(N{O_3})}_2}}\\limits_{Blue}  + 2Ag$$</p>\n<p>The solution of copper nitrate is blue in colour which is formed by the reaction of copper with silver nitrate.</p>\n<p>$$AgN{O_3} + NaCl \\to AgCl + NaN{O_3}$$</p>\n<p>silver chloride precipitates out (white colour ppt.) when silver nitrate reacts with sodium chloride (double displacement reaction).</p>\n<p>$$AgCl + 2N{H_4}OH \\to [Ag{(N{H_3})_2}]Cl + 2{H_2}O$$</p>\n<p>AgCl is soluble in NH<sub>4</sub>OH.</p>\n<p>$$Cu{(N{O_3})_2} + 4N{H_4}OH \\to [Cu{(N{H_3})_4}]{(N{O_3})_2} + 4{H_2}O$$</p>\n<p>Copper nitrate on reaction with ammonia or ammonium hydroxide gives intense blue solution which is due to $$[Cu{(N{H_3})_4}]$$.</p>"
        },
